         BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION

 IN THE MATTER OF THE APPLICATION OF EL                       )
 PASO ELECTRIC COMPANY FOR REVISION OF                        )
 ITS RETAIL ELECTRIC RATES PURSUANT TO                        )   Docket No. 25-00082-UT
 ADVICE NOTICE NO. 317                                        )

                     ORDER SETTING PREHEARING CONFERENCE

       THIS MATTER comes before Jocelyn Barrett and Elizabeth C. Hurst, appointed co-

hearing examiners, upon the application of El Paso Electric Company (“EPE”) for revision of its

retail electric rates pursuant to Advice Notice No. 317 (“Application”). The Hearing Examiners

FIND and CONCLUDE that a prehearing conference should be convened in this matter.

       IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

       A.     A prehearing conference will be held beginning at 10:00 a.m. on Thursday, April

16, 2026, via the Zoom platform.

       B.     Prior to the prehearing conference, counsel for EPE shall confer with the

prospective parties and attempt to reach agreement on a proposed schedule that includes dates

regarding any preliminary motions or issues.

       C.     Counsel for EPE should be ready to provide information regarding prospective

dates needed to accomplish the required notice.

       D.     EPE shall immediately e-mail the Application and supporting testimonies to the

Hearing Examiners.

       E.     By close of business on Monday, April 13, 2026, counsel for EPE shall e-mail the

Hearing Examiners its proposed procedural schedule and shall state the positions of Commission

Staff, any intervenors, and known potential parties on the proposed schedule.
                   BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order Setting Prehearing Conference                             Case Nos. 25-00082-UT


       F.      A Zoom invitation including the link to access the prehearing shall be sent to all

parties on the existing service list by Wednesday, April 15, 2026. If a party wishes to attend and

has not received the Zoom invitation with the link by that time, please contact Ana Kippenbrock

at ana.kippenbrock@prc.nm.gov.

       ISSUED under the seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, on April 3, 2026.




                        _________________________
                        Elizabeth C. Hurst
